#~
runtime.cpu.count is the number of CPUs this process may use, not the machine's.

A cluster job given 4 of a node's 64 cores, a container run with --cpus=2 and a
process started under taskset all see the whole machine through
hardware_concurrency(); sizing a thread pool from that starts 64 threads on 4
cores. The harness (run_vm_flag_tests.py) starts this program under
OBJECK_CPU_COUNT and, on Linux, under taskset, and compares the line it prints.
~#
class CpuCountAffinity {
  function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
    count := Runtime->GetProperty("runtime.cpu.count")->ToInt();
    "cpus={$count}"->PrintLine();
  }
}
